@startuml
title E10 - Verification, observability and release evidence
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #2877B5
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #17324D
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF1BF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9C6500
autonumber
actor "Development / test engineer" as Engineer
control "T01\nSimulation/CI" as T01
control "H02\nHub persistence" as H02
control "H08\nHub cloud link" as H08
control "B08\nOperations/data" as B08
boundary "A02\nApp home" as A02
control "T02\nHardware-in-loop tools" as T02
control "Physical four-node kit" as Devices
control "T03\nDeployment/operations" as T03
Engineer -> T01: Run contract, strict C++17, simulator, backend and app suites
T01 -> H02: Verify durability/idempotency invariants in host composition
T01 -> H08: Verify offline priority/replay scheduling
T01 -> B08: Verify tenant/audit/diagnostic domain behavior
T01 -> A02: Verify evidence versus connectivity presentation
Engineer -> T02: Run provisioning, RF, sensor, reset, flash and current tests
T02 -> Devices: Execute four-node physical fault/outage scenarios
Devices --> T02: Return measured, timestamped observations
Engineer -> T03: Deploy staging broker/database/providers and run restore drill
T03 -> B08: Collect independent alerts, backlogs and recovery evidence
B08 --> Engineer: Produce redacted release evidence bundle
note over T01,T03: Host green is necessary but not sufficient; release requires hardware, provider and installed-home evidence.
note over Engineer,T03: Outcome - Every release claim is tied to a repeatable test or operational record, with untested boundaries explicitly marked pending.
@enduml
